我希望我早知道这一点。

00:08:21.259 --> 00:08:22.860
That would have been something that would really have delighted me.
那真的会让我很高兴。

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:31.379
Even though I never read the Great Gatsby when I was supposed to, but about five years ago, I read it for the first time and I, you know, you read something and you feel like you've discovered it.
尽管我从未在应该读的时候读过《了不起的盖茨比》，但大约五年前，我第一次读到它，我，你知道，你读了一些东西，你感觉你已经发现了它。

00:08:31.379 --> 00:08:32.980
Has anyone heard of this book, The Great Gatsby?
有人听说过《了不起的盖茨比》这本书吗？

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.220
It's unbelievable.
真是难以置信。

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.100
I was like, you guys really should've made this.
我当时想，你们真的应该做这个。

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.820
I really did think it was an incredible book.
我确实认为这是一本不可思议的书。

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:43.659
But so I'm curious, so you and Carter, obviously you create these characters.
但我很好奇，显然是你和卡特创造了这些角色。

00:08:43.659 --> 00:08:44.500
You have this thing going.
你有这件事。

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.500
You've been ordered for 13 more episodes at Leet.
Leet 已为您订购了 13 集以上的剧集。

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.059
Well, you have this task ahead of you.
好吧，你面前有这个任务。

00:08:50.059 --> 00:09:03.460
What did the writers, what did you stumble upon in the room for episode two that felt really useful, like any eureka moments or like things that kind of made the story open up for you guys?
编剧们做了什么，你们在第二集的房间里偶然发现了什么感觉非常有用的东西，比如任何灵光一闪的时刻，或者类似让故事对你们开放的东西？

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:13.659
Yeah, I think the idea, because I think we were something, we're in the realm of like Ted throws a big party and it goes wrong and it's a big party episode.
是的，我认为这个想法，因为我认为我们是一些东西，我们就像特德举办了一场盛大的派对，但出了问题，这是一场盛大的派对插曲。

00:09:13.659 --> 00:09:19.419
And it felt, I remember feeling very afraid of that because party scenes are hard to write, they're hard to shoot.
我记得我感到非常害怕，因为派对场景很难写，也很难拍摄。

00:09:19.419 --> 00:09:23.899
If the whole episode takes place at one big party, there's that kind of like loss of energy, right?
如果整个情节发生在一个大型聚会上，就会有一种能量流失的感觉，对吧？

00:09:23.899 --> 00:09:26.700
There's this diffuse energy, there's all these extras.
有这种分散的能量，有所有这些额外的东西。

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.139
How do you make it feel like a himium episode?
你如何让它感觉像一个 hiium 剧集？

00:09:28.139 --> 00:09:33.620
like others, it comes, you do a party episode and it's all one big scene mostly and people pop in the shoe and pop in that room.
和其他人一样，它来了，你做了一个派对插曲，这主要是一个大场景，人们在鞋子里流行，在那个房间里流行。

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:40.419
It was worried, it didn't really feel like our show or our pilot, which was jumping around in time, lots of short scenes, cut, cut, cut.
它很担心，感觉不像我们的节目或试播集，它在时间上跳跃，有很多短场景，剪，剪，剪。

00:09:40.419 --> 00:09:44.019
So I think the spark was, it's three parties.
所以我认为火花是由三个政党组成的。

00:09:44.019 --> 00:09:54.899
It's three parties that sort of take place over three days and within that, we'll jump around a lot and we'll find ways to show that we're not just doing like it's a sitcom episode with a party and it's mostly set there.
这是三天内举行的三场派对，在这期间，我们会跳来跳去，我们会找到方法来表明我们不只是像情景喜剧剧集那样举办派对，而且大部分场景都在那里。

00:09:54.899 --> 00:10:04.539
I was thinking, I remember being very afraid of that, maybe like lose energy and seem more linear and, you know, like traditional if we did a party episode and episode two.
我在想，我记得我非常害怕这一点，也许会失去能量，看起来更线性，你知道，就像传统的，如果我们做了一个派对插曲和第二集。

00:10:04.539 --> 00:10:12.299
I remember always, even once we got the idea of chopping up into three parties, I remember I never quite shook the fear that like ass is just gonna be a wacky party episode.
我一直记得，即使我们有了分成三个派对的想法，我也记得我从未完全摆脱过这样的恐惧，即“像屁股”只会成为一个古怪的派对插曲。

00:10:12.299 --> 00:10:13.460
How do we make it different?
我们如何让它与众不同？

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.779
But right away in Act One, there's a bunch of playing with time, right?
但在第一幕中，就有很多时间游戏，对吧？

00:10:16.779 --> 00:10:18.779
There's like the fantasy of how the party's gonna go.
就像派对将如何进行的幻想。

00:10:18.779 --> 00:10:23.179
And we see Ted's fantasy and it's voiced over and Ted's voice is doing all the voices.
我们看到泰德的幻想，它是配音的，泰德的声音正在做所有的声音。

00:10:23.179 --> 00:10:29.500
It's great into Robyn's voice you know, et cetera, Robbins, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera, as Ted voiceover says that.
你知道，罗宾斯的声音很棒，等等，罗宾斯，等等，等等，等等，正如泰德画外音所说。

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:53.250
And then Barney interrupts and hijacks and it becomes Barney's fantasy and Ted turns to camera, breaks the fourth wall and says Barney, that was the moment to enact one of that episode and rewatching it, I really enjoyed that because it was like, that's the moment where it became a himium episode.
然后巴尼打断并劫持了它，这变成了巴尼的幻想，泰德转向镜头，打破了第四堵墙，说巴尼，那是表演其中一集并重新观看它的时刻，我真的很喜欢，因为它就像是，那是它成为一集的时刻。

00:10:53.250 --> 00:11:07.649
We'll be right back, and now, back's the show.
我们马上回来，现在，演出回来了。

00:11:07.649 --> 00:11:16.730
And that's another interesting thing about the show, while it's a very hard-on-its-sleeve, sincere show, it also had so many meta elements.
这是这部剧的另一个有趣之处，虽然它是一部非常严肃、真诚的剧，但它也有很多元元素。

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:28.129
Like, it was a TV show that was aware it was a TV show, and it was always like playing with structure and dancing it up and saying, or it was also aware of its own storytelling more than being a TV show.
就像，这是一个知道它是一个电视节目的电视节目，它总是喜欢玩弄结构，跳舞并说，或者它也比电视节目更了解自己的故事讲述。

00:11:28.129 --> 00:11:38.450
You know, like, like, okay, we're gonna show you what he's clearly just saying at the bar, but we're gonna kind of flip it on his head and someone's gonna interrupt someone else's.
你知道，就像，好吧，我们会向你展示他在酒吧里清楚地说了什么，但我们会把它翻转到他的头上，有人会打断别人的。

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:42.250
They're just gonna like hijack someone's story in the middle of the story.
他们只是喜欢在故事中间劫持某人的故事。

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.690
I don't know, it's quite clever in that way.
我不知道，这很聪明。

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:44.529
I love that moment.
我喜欢那一刻。

00:11:44.529 --> 00:11:47.330
I love, I forgot about Ted breaking the fourth wall.
我爱，我忘记了泰德打破第四堵墙。

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:51.889
I forgot about like, you turn to camera and you just start talking to Barney through the TV screen.
我忘记了，你转向镜头，然后开始通过电视屏幕与巴尼交谈。

00:11:51.889 --> 00:11:54.970
I forgot about the lip syncing where Ted is his voice.
我忘记了口型同步，特德是他的声音。

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.529
You know, with all the other characters, I love that so much.
你知道，和所有其他角色一样，我非常喜欢这一点。

00:11:57.529 --> 00:12:03.210
Josh, I just wanna ask you a question about the show.
乔什，我只是想问你一个关于这个节目的问题。

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:06.730
So you get the pilot, you're on it.
所以你得到了飞行员，你就可以了。

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.370
You're actually making a pilot.
你实际上是在培养一名飞行员。

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.450
Then this show gets picked up.
然后这个节目就被收看了。

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:27.399
Now your life, you know, you hear stories out here of people who like move from across the country to be in this TV show they got and then it gets canceled a couple of episodes in or you give up your waiting, you know, your server job.
现在，你知道，你的生活中，你听到一些故事，人们喜欢从全国各地搬来参加他们得到的这个电视节目，然后它被取消了几集，或者你放弃了等待，你知道，你的服务器工作。

00:12:27.399 --> 00:12:27.899
job.
工作。

00:12:27.899 --> 00:12:29.906
You know, have a show.
你知道，有表演。

00:12:29.906 --> 00:12:31.731
Do you take that in?
你接受吗？

00:12:31.731 --> 00:12:35.015
Can you not think of it in that way?
你能不这样想吗？

00:12:34.879 --> 00:12:36.337
And do you just have to know to the grind?
你只需要知道到底吗？

00:12:36.337 --> 00:12:37.759
So now I'm going to do this next episode.
所以现在我要在下一集做这个。

00:12:37.759 --> 00:12:41.020
And we're going to we're going to hope for the best.
我们将抱最好的希望。

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:45.535
What were you feeling now that maybe your life was changing quite a bit?
也许你的生活发生了很大的变化，你现在有什么感觉？

00:12:45.535 --> 00:12:53.059
Well, it's tricky because you don't want to pop the champagne and kill the champagne until you can afford the champagne.
嗯，这很棘手，因为你不想开香槟并杀死香槟，直到你买得起香槟。

00:12:53.059 --> 00:13:06.979
You know, I do remember My first agent, she signed me right out of grad school at NYU and I lived in New York for a while, but I was generally living mostly in LA and then I go back to New York in the summer and do a play.
你知道，我确实记得我的第一个经纪人，她在纽约大学研究生院毕业后就签下了我，我在纽约住了一段时间，但我通常大部分时间住在洛杉矶，然后我在夏天回到纽约演出。

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:18.120
I was a little bit by Coswise, mostly living in New York and I had done a bunch of pilots and she always got me what's called a relocation fee because she said, no, he lives in New York, you have to pay to relocate him to LA.
我有点喜欢 Coswise，主要住在纽约，我做过很多试点，她总是给我所谓的搬迁费，因为她说，不，他住在纽约，你必须付费才能把他搬到洛杉矶。

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:33.779
She always built it into my deal and she told me on how I met your mother, she had negotiated for me with this dealmaker before, and she tried to get the relocation fee and the dealmaker said, Rhonda, we know he lives in LA, knock it off, you know, like they weren't gonna, they weren't gonna give it to him.
她总是把它纳入我的交易中，她告诉我我是如何认识你母亲的，她之前曾为我与这个交易撮合者谈判过，她试图获得搬迁费，而交易撮合者说，朗达，我们知道他住在洛杉矶，结束吧，你知道，就像他们不会那样，他们不会给他。

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:34.779
Yeah.
是的。

00:13:34.779 --> 00:13:42.860
So I was still in this $750 a month sublet, I was subletting for my friend Megan, a college friend of mine.
所以我仍然住在这个每月 750 美元的转租中，我是为我的朋友梅根转租的，她是我的大学朋友。

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:46.820
I didn't move until second season, I think.
我想直到第二季我才搬家。

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.740
So I kept things real modest.
所以我保持谦虚。

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:53.100
We lived right around, my best friends lived across the street.
我们就住在附近，我最好的朋友住在街对面。

00:13:53.100 --> 00:14:00.340
We lived right by the CBS like main kind of corporate building where they shoot the prices right and all these other like television city.
我们住在哥伦比亚广播公司旁边，就像主要的企业大楼一样，他们在那里制定正确的价格，所有其他就像电视城一样。

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:01.340
Is that what it's called on Beverly?
这就是贝弗利的名字吗？

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.340
Television city, yeah.
电视城啊

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:03.340
And do you remember this Craig?
你还记得这个克雷格吗？

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:06.720
They put up a huge how I met your mother.
他们大肆宣传我是如何认识你母亲的。

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.720
It was the lip couch.
这是嘴唇沙发。

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:12.159
It was me on the lip couch with the other four behind me.
我坐在沙发上，其他四个人在我身后。

00:14:12.159 --> 00:14:15.519
And they put it up and they kept it up the entire season.
他们坚持了这一点，并在整个赛季都保持了这种状态。

00:14:15.519 --> 00:14:16.759
They didn't take it down.
他们没有把它拿下来。

00:14:16.759 --> 00:14:26.000
So I was always walking on Beverly Boulevard with my friends and it was just like this enormous mural of us on the side of this building on Beverly Boulevard.
所以我总是和朋友们一起走在比佛利大道上，就像比佛利大道这座建筑一侧的一幅巨大的壁画一样。

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.360
I didn't know that was right under this, basically.
基本上我不知道就在这下面。

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:29.360
That was really funny.
那真的很有趣。

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:41.019
So that was one of the things where life just felt a little like there was this, this like tincture of weirdness, like a solution of weirdness that got dropped into whatever I was living in.
所以这就是生活感觉有点像有这样的事情之一，就像奇怪的酊剂，就像一种奇怪的解决方案融入到我所生活的一切中。

00:14:41.019 --> 00:14:43.960
And suddenly it was like, this is a little bit weirder.
突然间，这有点奇怪了。

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:48.120
And then my friend Amy was like, oh, I forgot that like people are going to watch the show.
然后我的朋友艾米说，哦，我忘了人们会看这个节目。

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:54.679
We're going to go out with you and it's going to add a whole other element to our lives of people coming up and saying things to you or wanting a picture or whatever.
我们将和你一起出去，这将为我们的生活添加一个全新的元素，人们会走过来对你说话或想要一张照片或其他什么。

00:14:54.679 --> 00:14:56.200
And it wasn't out of control back then.
而且当时还没有失控。

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.039
It was still we were finding our feet.
我们仍然在寻找立足点。

00:14:58.039 --> 00:15:06.879
So I definitely had this feeling that there was the potential of my life getting kind of disorienting and strange and fun, you know.
所以我确实有这样的感觉，我的生活有可能变得有点迷失方向、变得奇怪和有趣，你知道。

00:15:06.879 --> 00:15:13.840
I remember Julie who was one of our, the CBS executive, Julie, who is great.
我记得朱莉是我们哥伦比亚广播公司的高管之一，朱莉很棒。

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.639
Hello, Julie, if you're listening.
你好，朱莉，如果你在听的话。

00:15:15.639 --> 00:15:21.399
But Julie, I remember the premiere party saying, she said, how are you feeling?
但是朱莉，我记得首映式派对上她说，你感觉怎么样？

00:15:21.399 --> 00:15:23.039
And I said, I'm nervous.
我说，我很紧张。

00:15:23.039 --> 00:15:25.519
And she said, why?
她说，为什么？

00:15:25.519 --> 00:15:29.309
And I said, I'm just nervous for people to like, know who I am.
我说，我只是担心人们喜欢、知道我是谁。

00:15:29.309 --> 00:15:31.470
And she said, I said, what's it going to be like?
她说，我说，那会是什么样子？

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:35.110
And she said, people are going to want pictures and you'll get good tables at restaurants.
她说，人们会想要拍照，你会在餐馆找到好桌子。

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:36.309
It's not that bad.
没那么糟糕。

00:15:36.309 --> 00:15:38.350
You know what you're just like?
你知道你是什么样的人吗？

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.669
It's fine.
没关系。

00:15:39.669 --> 00:15:40.909
That's really funny.
这真的很有趣。

00:15:40.909 --> 00:15:43.750
And you may have found some stuff there.
您可能在那里找到了一些东西。

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.549
But yeah, she did leave out some stuff.
但是，是的，她确实遗漏了一些东西。

00:15:46.549 --> 00:15:52.029
But I definitely had this sense like, like I said, I got fired from my first pilot.
但我确实有这种感觉，就像我说的，我被第一个飞行员解雇了。

00:15:52.029 --> 00:15:55.350
The second one got canceled very quickly after a couple of episodes.
第二集在几集之后很快就被取消了。

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.269
The third one didn't get picked up by NBC.
第三个没有被 NBC 接收。

00:15:57.269 --> 00:15:59.629
Like I'd had everything happen to me but a hit show.
就像除了热门节目之外一切都发生在我身上一样。

00:15:59.629 --> 00:16:06.990
So I kind of felt like, I don't know why I felt this way, but I was like, well, the odds are such that and I had a good feeling about it.
所以我有点感觉，我不知道为什么我有这种感觉，但我想，好吧，可能性就是这样，而且我对此有很好的感觉。

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.149
Like I said, at the end of the pilot.
就像我说的，在试播集结束时。

00:16:08.149 --> 00:16:12.309
So I knew something was good and cool about the show.
所以我知道这个节目有一些很好而且很酷的东西。

00:16:12.309 --> 00:16:16.899
What was strange was we shot the pilot in March.
奇怪的是我们在三月份枪杀了飞行员。

00:16:16.899 --> 00:16:17.740
Something like that.
类似的事情。

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:21.899
I think we shot the pilot in March and then you end up shooting this in July, August.
我想我们在三月拍摄了试播集，然后你最终在七月、八月拍摄了这个。

00:16:21.899 --> 00:16:23.179
August, probably, yeah.
八月，可能吧，是的。

00:16:23.179 --> 00:16:27.700
But it's really, it's a couple days later, but you've had a couple months in between.
但实际上，这是几天后的事情，但中间已经有几个月了。

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:28.519
You had a couple months.
你有几个月的时间。

00:16:28.519 --> 00:16:33.340
You found out it's picked up in May and then you have you start shooting in maybe early August or something, whatever.
你发现它是在五月份开始拍摄的，然后你可能会在八月初或者其他什么时候开始拍摄。

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.179
Yeah.
是的。

00:16:34.179 --> 00:16:39.860
So, you know, it was like kind of like, okay, we're back, isn't this cool?
所以，你知道，就像是，好吧，我们回来了，这不是很酷吗？

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:54.379
But I was talking to a friend of mine last night who has a really cool theater opportunity in New York and he said, I'm nervous about going on the dopamine roller coaster when it gets announced and everyone's out, you know, saying, this is so great and how exciting and I just wanna stay balanced.
但昨晚我和我的一个朋友聊天，他在纽约有一个非常酷的戏剧机会，他说，当它宣布并且每个人都出去时，我对乘坐多巴胺过山车感到紧张，你知道，说，这太棒了，多么令人兴奋，我只是想保持平衡。

00:16:54.379 --> 00:17:09.740
And I told him I said, I've had a lot of cool things happen in my career and I was so afraid of seeming arrogant or out of touch or cocky in front of my friends who weren't at working that I didn't allow myself to enjoy things.
